  m_Name: Tuyaux_Tuyaux_0_0
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Exhaust Manifold
  description: The Exhaust Manifold is a medium-sized, complex-shaped component located
    at the top-center-center of the rocket engine, constructed from a Tuyaux material.
    Its primary function is to collect and direct exhaust gases away from the engine's
    cylinders, minimizing backpressure and maximizing engine efficiency. An interesting
    detail about the Exhaust Manifold is that its design must accommodate the high-temperature
    and high-pressure exhaust gases, while also providing a stable and durable connection
    to the engine's exhaust system.
